1
00:00:00,190 --> 00:00:02,128
If a baby turns their head away while

2
00:00:02,128 --> 00:00:03,495
you're playing, don't try to get

3
00:00:03,495 --> 00:00:04,690
their attention.

4
00:00:04,690 --> 00:00:06,474
Most of us get right in their face

5
00:00:06,474 --> 00:00:09,370
at that moment and make even more noise.

6
00:00:09,370 --> 00:00:10,990
We think they're bored, or that they've

7
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:12,320
lost interest.

8
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,540
But it's actually the opposite.

9
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:16,533
A baby's brain can only process

10
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:17,980
a few things at once.

11
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:20,300
Your face, your voice, your expressions

12
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,670
fill it up within seconds.

13
00:00:22,670 --> 00:00:24,159
Turning their head doesn't mean

14
00:00:24,159 --> 00:00:25,740
"I'm bored of you."

15
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:28,393
It means "Hold on, there's too much

16
00:00:28,393 --> 00:00:30,300
going on, I need to breathe."

17
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,184
If you don't chase them right then,

18
00:00:32,184 --> 00:00:34,722
and give them a few seconds of space,

19
00:00:34,722 --> 00:00:36,102
their heart rate slows down

20
00:00:36,102 --> 00:00:37,540
and they calm down.

21
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:39,840
And soon, they'll come back on their own.

22
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:42,195
Because for a baby who can't talk yet,

23
00:00:42,195 --> 00:00:43,592
the quietest way to say "break"

24
00:00:43,592 --> 00:00:45,640
is to look away.

